// Drives haze-notes' vault indexing (src/vault.hz) over a folder of awkward
// names and checks the tree comes out in exactly technicalsketcher.web's
// order. That order is folders first, then names starting with a date
// (DD.MM.YYYY or DD-MM-YYYY) oldest first, then everything else by ICU's
// German collation with numbers compared by value. Ties keep the order the
// folder was listed in, which node lists in byte order.
//
// `expectedOrder` is not written by hand: it is what technicalsketcher.web's
// own compareEntries (cut verbatim out of src/components/store.ts) produced
// for this exact fixture, run by Electron 42 (ICU 78.2) the way its Electron
// build reads a vault. Some of what it pins down:
//   - JavaScript Date arithmetic: 31.02.2024 is 2 March, month 00 is
//     December of the year before, day 00 the last day of the month before,
//     years 0000-0099 are 1900-1999, 12.03.20245 is a date (12.03.2024),
//     and so is a name that is nothing but one (a folder "24.12.2023");
//   - equal dates fall back to byte order, not to the name order
//     ("12.03.2024 Bio" < "12.03.2024 Physik" < "12.03.2024 analysis");
//   - names that collate equal ("a001", "a01", "a1"; "Blatt 02", "Blatt 2")
//     go by byte order too;
//   - case and accents only break ties ("mathe" < "Mathe", "Ubung" <
//     "übung" < "Übung"), umlauts sort with their base letter, ß after ss;
//   - spaces < punctuation < symbols < digits < letters.
//
// haze-notes is an executable, so nothing can depend on it: run this from a
// throwaway exe project inside the repository that depends on unicode, with
// src/vault.hz copied in verbatim and this file as its main.hz.

ref struct State {
    checks: int = 0;
    failures: int = 0;

    mut fn check(name: str, ok: bool) {
        this.checks = this.checks + 1;
        if !ok {
            this.failures = this.failures + 1;
            fmt.println(f"FAIL: {name}");
        }
    }
}

